# Tower Clash — Android upload keystore request (MM-13, docs/MOBILE.md §6 "Android", path A).
#
# Pushing a change of this file to the branch claude/tower-war-game-plan-weqwpb starts
# .github/workflows/tower-clash-android-keystore.yml once. Pushes to any other branch start
# nothing. The run stops in its first step, "Check secrets", while the repository secret
# ANDROID_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD is missing (the stakeholder creates it: "parol sirrini əlavə etdim").
# With the password it makes the upload key and keeps it for 1 day as the artifact
# "android-upload-keystore"; the stakeholder copies its text into the secret
# ANDROID_KEYSTORE_BASE64 the same day.
#
# The same workflow also runs when its own .yml file is pushed, and "Re-run all jobs" on any of
# its runs (Safari) works too; such runs read THIS file as it was in that commit.
#
# Keys (one key=value per line; lines starting with # are ignored; unknown keys are an error):
#   generate          yes — make the key; no — the run only reads this file and stops (required)
#   replace_existing  no (default) — refuse when ANDROID_KEYSTORE_BASE64 already exists
#                     yes — make a new key anyway; after the first Play upload a new key also
#                           needs a Play "upload key reset" (docs/MOBILE.md §6)
#   note              free text for the log, at most 200 characters
#   requested         UTC time of the request, e.g. 2026-10-09T15:30:00Z — change it every time
generate=yes
replace_existing=no
note=MM-13 first request: expected to stop at the secrets check until the stakeholder adds ANDROID_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD
requested=2026-10-09T18:00:00Z
